    "frage": "¿Qué le compras a Pablo?",
    "antwortKacheln": ["le / les", "comprar", "(yo)", "un reloj"],
    "antwort": "Le compro un reloj."
  },
  "tandemSoGehts": [
    "Cut the cards in the middle. Partner A takes the left half, Partner B takes the right half.",
    "A builds question 1 from the tiles and asks it: “¿Qué le regalas a tu madre?”",
    "B hears the question and builds the answer. A tile like “le / les” means: choose! One person → le, more than one → les; me / te and nos / os work the same way. The pronoun goes before the verb. If you also use lo, la, los or las, le and les become se: Se las doy. A tile in brackets like (yo) says who is speaking: it is not written.",
    "Then B asks question 2 and A answers. Take turns. At the end, check with the answer sheet.",
    "Last, swap cards and do it all again, faster."
  ],
  "tandemRedemittel": [
    { "p1": "Número 1: ¿Qué le …?", "p2": "Le … (a mi madre)." },
    { "p1": "¿Le o les?", "p2": "Les: son varias personas." },
    { "p1": "Perdona, ¿puedes repetir, por favor?", "p2": "Número 2: ¿A quién le …?" }
  ],
